{"title":"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Lightning_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Lightning Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Big Al, the ape, ate 100 bananas from May 1 through May 5. Each day he ate six more bananas than on the previous day. How many bananas did Big Al eat on May 5?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/845cf18e96b8e9d73e32e70c66877af2d3e47fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 22\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 30\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 32\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days from May 1 to May 5. The number of bananas he eats each day is an arithmetic sequence. He eats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> bananas on May 5, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/994cf494751c6e56f26411627078ca5cef5a388e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-4(6)=n-24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> bananas on May 1. The sum of this arithmetic sequence is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c68fe9ac7186162e3c2cd0f7c5117b0d1ea9ef2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{n+n-24}{2} \\cdot 5 &amp;= 100\\\\ n-12&amp;=20\\\\ n&amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 32} \\end{align*}\" width=\"198\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days from May 1 to May 5. If we set the first day as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the second day can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/04901235ff573c150d7bedafe9510525f1ace480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, the third as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/492cb89c2c985eb88d96c8b080b9b6c395b20d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, and so on, for five days. \nThe sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff2e61dadd23c2768d20e23a7ce748bb7dc9347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+(n+6)+(n+12)+(n+18)+(n+24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, as stated in the problem. We can write a very simple equation, that is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e126515c58b8dde59c175cb5e1fc2ca6150a2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5n+60=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />.\nNow all we do is just solve. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a8fc710ab1640bec62e6b130461f9904b95959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5n=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, so Big Al eats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bananas on the first day. The fifth day, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8bed7d55c9e33e7ee77c1b4fb3e547a7d4d7b60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which is your answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Lightning_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Lightning_Quick)\">Solution 3 (Lightning Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Lightning Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Simply realize that the middle term of the arithmetic sequence is the arithmetic mean of all terms, which is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6bd3cff48114b8cce3b212a7fb0ca7596573e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100}{5}=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />. This means that the number of bananas the ape ate on May 5th is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c7ed52041f2d3ec3baa79ebdee5de1872ec4d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+6*2=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />. Select <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>You can do this quicker than you read it if you truly master arithmetic sequences.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8\">2005 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205015\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 169/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3709/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.417      1 -total\n 58.36%    7.247      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 39.12%    4.858      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11642:|#|:idhash:canonical and times